The horizon behaves differently because its comoving coordinate distance from Alice is not fixed. From the $45^\circ$ null line ending at $T=0$, the horizon distance on a slice of constant $T<0$ is $\Delta x_H=-T=\frac{1}{H}e^{-Ht}.$ Multiplying by the scale factor gives $D_H(t)=a(t)\Delta x_H
=e^{Ht}\frac{e^{-Ht}}{H}
=\frac{1}{H}.$ Restoring units, $D_H=c/H$. The coordinate gap shrinks, the metric scale grows, and their product remains constant.

